From e83b0af408551e675606032651a949d60329417a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2015 00:16:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: Try harder to connect to known networks

Raise FAVORITE_MAXIMUM_RETRIES from 2 to 4. For a favourite network a
failed 4-way handshake is retried up to this many times before ConnMan
concludes the passphrase is wrong and reports invalid-key. Some WiFi
drivers shipped on OSMC devices fail the handshake transiently,
especially straight after boot, and two attempts are not enough.

Signed-off-by: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
---
 plugins/wifi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugins/wifi.c b/plugins/wifi.c
index 9ce7b5a3..8660cd88 100644
--- a/plugins/wifi.c
+++ b/plugins/wifi.c
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 
 #define CLEANUP_TIMEOUT   8	/* in seconds */
 #define INACTIVE_TIMEOUT  12	/* in seconds */
-#define FAVORITE_MAXIMUM_RETRIES 2
+#define FAVORITE_MAXIMUM_RETRIES 4
 
 #define BGSCAN_DEFAULT "simple:30:-65:300"
 #define AUTOSCAN_EXPONENTIAL "exponential:3:300"
-- 
2.34.1

